        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-016",
          "ruleIndex": 52,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "nginx/nginx.conf and nginx/nginx-tls.conf have no limit_req or limit_conn directives. A distributed attack sending thousands of requests to /api/auth/login from a single IP can exhaust the application process before the in-memory rate limiter can record and reject the requests, since the limiter only activates at the Python layer."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "nginx/nginx.conf",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 6,
                  "endLine": 26,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 1,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "server {\n    listen 80;\n    server_name _;\n    client_max_body_size 50m;\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass http://homeschool_app;\n        ...\n    }\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "category": "rate-limiting"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "Add nginx rate limiting: limit_req_zone $binary_remote_addr zone=auth:10m rate=5r/m; and limit_req zone=auth burst=10 nodelay; on the /api/auth/login and /api/auth/register location blocks. Add limit_conn_zone for general connection limiting."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-770",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-017",
          "ruleIndex": 53,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "main.py lines 573-582: api_capabilities() is in the GENERAL_RATE_LIMIT exclusion list, returns capability registry state publicly, and includes 'auth' providers via get_auth_providers(). An attacker learns exactly which auth paths (OIDC, SAML, local) are enabled, which AI providers are running, and which optional features are available."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "backend/main.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 573,
                  "endLine": 582,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 60,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "@app.get(f'{API_PREFIX}/capabilities')\nasync def api_capabilities() -> dict[str, object]:\n    capabilities = await get_capability_registry().check_all()\n    disabled = [name for name, state in capabilities.items() if not state['enabled']]\n    return {\n        'status': 'degraded' if disabled else 'ok',\n        'capabilities': capabilities,\n        'optional_unavailable': disabled,\n        'auth': get_auth_providers(),\n    }"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "category": "info-disclosure"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "Move detailed capability data behind authentication, returning only the auth_providers list publicly (needed for the login UI). Authenticated users can receive the full capability breakdown."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-200",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-018",
          "ruleIndex": 54,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "config.py line 59: jwt_secret: str = Field('', ...). startup.py validates that exactly one of JWT_JWKS_URL or JWT_SECRET is set when JWT_ENABLED=true (line 184), but does not validate that JWT_SECRET meets a minimum entropy requirement (e.g., 32 random bytes). A secret of 'test' or 'password' would be accepted."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "backend/startup.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 178,
                  "endLine": 192,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 80,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "def _validate_jwt_config(config: Settings) -> None:\n    if not config.jwt_enabled:\n        return\n    has_jwks = bool(config.jwt_jwks_url.strip())\n    has_secret = bool(config.jwt_secret.strip())\n    if has_jwks == has_secret:\n        raise StartupValidationError('JWT auth requires exactly one of JWT_JWKS_URL or JWT_SECRET ...')"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "category": "jwt"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "In _validate_jwt_config(), when has_secret is True add: if len(config.jwt_secret.strip()) < 32: raise StartupValidationError('JWT_SECRET must be at least 32 characters'). Also add JWT_SECRET to the _PLACEHOLDER_SECRETS set."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-321",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-019",
          "ruleIndex": 55,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "nginx/nginx-tls.conf line 33: Strict-Transport-Security header is 'max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains' without 'preload'. The application-level HSTS in main.py (line 225-230) also defaults hsts_preload=False. First-time HTTPS visitors are not protected against SSL stripping attacks."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "nginx/nginx-tls.conf",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 33,
                  "endLine": 33,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 70,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "add_header Strict-Transport-Security \"max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains\" always;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "category": "tls"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "After ensuring the domain is stable and TLS is working correctly, add 'preload' to the HSTS header: Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload. Submit the domain to the HSTS preload list at https://hstspreload.org/. Also set HSTS_PRELOAD=true in the application config."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-319",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-020",
          "ruleIndex": 56,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "auth.py lines 340-344: oidc_verify() is in PUBLIC_API_PATHS and returns OIDCVerifyResponse which includes configured, reachable, discovery_url, issuer, and authorization_endpoint. An attacker learns the OIDC provider's full endpoint configuration even before authenticating."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "backend/routers/auth.py",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 340,
                  "endLine": 344,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 70,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "@router.get('/oidc/verify', response_model=OIDCVerifyResponse)\nasync def oidc_verify() -> JSONResponse:\n    verification = await verify_oidc_configuration()\n    status_code = status.HTTP_200_OK if verification['reachable'] else status.HTTP_503_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE\n    return JSONResponse(status_code=status_code, content=verification)"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "category": "info-disclosure"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "Move the OIDC verify endpoint behind authentication or restrict it to admin users. Alternatively, return only a boolean reachable status without the full OIDC endpoint URLs in the public response."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-200",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "DAST-CONFIG-021",
          "ruleIndex": 57,
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "nginx/nginx.conf line 10 and nginx-tls.conf line 31: client_max_body_size 50m. backend/config.py line 85: upload_max_bytes defaults to 25MB (25 * 1024 * 1024). Requests between 25-50MB waste nginx buffer, backend process memory, and database connection time before being rejected with 413."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "nginx/nginx.conf",
                  "uriBaseId": "%SRCROOT%"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 10,
                  "endLine": 10,
                  "startColumn": 1,
                  "endColumn": 30,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "client_max_body_size 50m;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "category": "api-auth"
          },
          "fixes": [
            {
              "description": {
                "text": "Align nginx client_max_body_size with UPLOAD_MAX_BYTES (set both to 26m to account for multipart overhead). This fails large uploads at the nginx layer before the app processes them, reducing DoS attack surface."
              }
            }
          ],
          "taxa": [
            {
              "id": "CWE-770",
              "toolComponent": {
                "name": "CWE"
              }
            }
          ]
